        "title": "DOJ reportedly demands Apple and Google identify over 100,000 users of car app",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/doj-reportedly-demands-apple-and-google-identify-over-100000-users-of-car-app/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/08/app-store-ios-26.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>According to a new report from <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/thomasbrewster/2026/05/14/government-demands-apple-and-google-identify-over-100000-users-of-car-app/\"><em>Forbes</em></a>, the Department of Justice is demanding Apple, Amazon, and Google hand over “identities, addresses, and purchase histories” of more than 100,000 users of a “car tinkering app” called EZ Lynk.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl,app-store\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052393\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/doj-reportedly-demands-apple-and-google-identify-over-100000-users-of-car-app/#more-1052393\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
