        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/why-i-use-apple-calendar-and-not-a-to-do-list-as-my-task-manager/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/Why-I-use-Apple-Calendar-and-not-a-to-do-list-as-my-task-manager.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>A to-do list feels like one of those things that almost everyone on the planet has, be it an old school one handwritten in a paper notebook or some kind of app. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Personally, however, I don’t have any kind of conventional to-do list. Instead, for decades now, I’ve been in the habit of using a calendar as my to-do list, and here are the reasons you too might want to give this a try …</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-calendar,reminders\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052206\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/why-i-use-apple-calendar-and-not-a-to-do-list-as-my-task-manager/#more-1052206\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
