        "title": "Apple Card’s transition to Chase: Here’s what’s not changing (and might be)",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/14/apple-cards-transition-to-chase-heres-whats-not-changing-and-might-be/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2024/10/apple-card-fi.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Apple Card is <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/01/07/apple-confirms-chase-takeover-for-apple-card-and-reveals-new-details/\">officially moving to Chase</a>, with Apple’s current partner Goldman Sachs transitioning out over the next year or two. Apple has <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/02/12/apple-card-is-moving-to-chase-heres-everything-we-know/\">published details</a> on what to expect during the transition, here’s everything the company says won’t change once Chase takes over—and a few things that might.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-card,chase\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1047419\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/14/apple-cards-transition-to-chase-heres-whats-not-changing-and-might-be/#more-1047419\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
