        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/14/psa-a-security-breach-means-you-must-update-the-chatgpt-mac-app/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/A-security-breach-means-you-must-update-the-ChatGPT-Mac-app.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>If you use the <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/chatgpt/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">ChatGPT</a> desktop app on <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/mac/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Mac</a>, you’ll be forced to update it sometime between now and June 12. That’s due to a <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/security/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">security</a> breach involving two OpenAI employee devices … </p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"chatgpt,mac,openai,security\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052162\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/14/psa-a-security-breach-means-you-must-update-the-chatgpt-mac-app/#more-1052162\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
