        "title": "Two AI video iPhone apps are going viral after rising from the ashes of OpenAI’s Sora",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/13/new-ai-video-generation-apps-are-rising-from-the-ashes-of-openais-sora/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/09/sora-app-icon.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Back in March, OpenAI abruptly pulled the plug on its Sora video app. Two months later, a pair of AI video generation apps is competing for the top of the App Store.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"ai,app-store,apps,iphone\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052003\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/13/new-ai-video-generation-apps-are-rising-from-the-ashes-of-openais-sora/#more-1052003\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
