        "title": "Court grants Musk’s bid to add Craig Federighi to Apple/OpenAI lawsuit, spares Cook",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/court-grants-musks-bid-to-add-craig-federighi-to-apple-openai-lawsuit-spares-cook/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/10/Apple-asks-judge-to-dismiss-absurd-AI-claim-by-Elon-Musk.webp?w=1500\" /></div><p>Apple’s Senior Vice President of Software Engineering, Craig Federighi, has been added as a document custodian in xAI’s antitrust lawsuit against Apple and OpenAI. Here’s what that means.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl,openai,xai\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1052438\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/15/court-grants-musks-bid-to-add-craig-federighi-to-apple-openai-lawsuit-spares-cook/#more-1052438\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
